From a0a819d4219dbf76a6c6ccc0dc4fd9b277db0e7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:12:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SurfaceFlinger: only keep an external off client composition
 while the HAL mirrors

Being on layer stack 0 is not the same as being mirrored. A 4K/ultra external
runs direct-link, needs its own client composition, and was getting none --
which is why the runtime `persist.sys.xdplus.mirror_no_client=0` override had to
be set by hand on that path.

The composer now publishes `sys.xdplus.hwc_mirroring`, carrying only the mirror
refusals that do not depend on this display's own composition. The refusals that
do read SurfaceFlinger's output are deliberately left out: feeding those back
into this decision would oscillate.

Changes:
- `Display.cpp`: gate `isMirroringExternal()` on `sys.xdplus.hwc_mirroring`, read live so it follows a hotplug or a mode change

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Id8a00e0500c9868da709aa4cdb800be698785ffb
---
 .../surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp   | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
index da6dbaa830..dfe9558795 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
@@ -302,7 +302,15 @@ bool Display::isMirroringExternal() const {
     }
     static const bool enabled =
             property_get_bool("persist.sys.xdplus.mirror_no_client", true);
-    return enabled;
+    if (!enabled) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    // Being on layer stack 0 is not the same as being mirrored: a 4K/ultra
+    // external runs direct-link and needs its own client composition. The
+    // composer publishes whether it will mirror at all; only its decisions
+    // that do not depend on this display's composition are in there.
+    // Read live -- it changes on hotplug and on a mode change.
+    return property_get_bool("sys.xdplus.hwc_mirroring", true);
 }
 
 bool Display::getSkipColorTransform() const {
